Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:51:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Trace=1: submit observer for the FG command buffer

Diagnostics only; nothing here runs unless vk-present-adapter.ini sets
Trace=1, and the original submit receives every argument unchanged.

- fg-submit-observation.h: a bounded CPU observer. It records which
  ReShade command events were seen on a command buffer between its
  init/reset and the first DLSS-G evaluate recorded into it (8 samples,
  512 command buffers), and in which vkQueueSubmit/vkQueueSubmit2 batch
  that command buffer was submitted.
- fg-trace.inc: register the command events, read the caller's submit
  arrays under SEH so an unreadable array cannot strand a lock or drop the
  submit, bound the pNext walk, suppress nested observation, and log a
  summary that states what the observation cannot prove (missed native
  commands, GPU readiness). The per-batch preview, and with it the
  per-queue timeline count, is parsed only while the 8-sample window is
  open; batch, command-buffer, wait and signal totals come from the full
  traversal.
- tests/vulkan-fg-relay/test-fg-trace.cpp: expect the preview-window rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
